{
  "analysis": "I'm in the /workspace directory which contains a registry folder, registry.json, and some documentation files. I need to understand the structure and available tools before creating the agent audit report.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace by reading the README_INPUT.txt, examining registry.json, checking what's in the registry folder, and looking at skill_context to understand the available tools and expected format.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat README_INPUT.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat registry.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la registry/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the registry.json contains 4 agents: security-auditor, code-reviewer, docs-helper, and auth-debugger. Two agents (security-auditor and auth-debugger) mention security/authentication in their descriptions. I need to check the skill_context files for the expected output format and any specific tools to use.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md and manifest.json files from skill_context to understand the expected format and tools for creating the audit report.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la registry/agents/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md describes registry tools (list.js, search.js, get.js) that should be used for agent discovery. I need to find where these tools are located and use them to discover agents rather than scanning folders directly.",
  "plan": "Look for the registry tools (bin directory) and examine the agent files in registry/agents/. Then use the registry tools to discover agents and create the audit report.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "find . -name '*.js' -o -name 'bin' -type d 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la registry/agents/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat registry/agents/security-auditor.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The heredoc is having issues with newline characters inside the string. Let me try a different approach - writing the Python script using printf with proper escaping.",
  "plan": "Use printf to write the Python script to a file, then execute it.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -f audit_script.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' 'import json' 'import re' '' 'with open(\"registry.json\", \"r\") as f:' '    registry = json.load(f)' '' 'agents = registry[\"agents\"]' 'audit_results = []' 'security_auth_agents = []' '' 'for agent in agents:' '    name = agent[\"name\"]' '    description = agent[\"description\"].lower()' '    has_security = bool(re.search(r\"security|authentication|auth\", description))' '    agent_info = {' \"        'name': name,\" \"        'description': agent['description'],\" \"        'path': agent['path'],\" \"        'flags_security_auth': has_security\" '    }' '    audit_results.append(agent_info)' '    if has_security:' '        security_auth_agents.append(name)' '' 'audit_json = {' \"    'total_agents': len(agents),\" \"    'agents': audit_results,\" \"    'security_auth_flags': security_auth_agents\" '}' '' 'with open(\"agent_audit.json\", \"w\") as f:' '    json.dump(audit_json, f, indent=2)' '' 'print(\"Created agent_audit.json\")' > audit_script.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat audit_script.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The Python script was created successfully. Now I need to run it to generate agent_audit.json, then add the summary.txt generation.",
  "plan": "Run the audit script to create agent_audit.json, then append the summary generation code and run again.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 audit_script.py\\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat agent_audit.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "agent_audit.json was created successfully with all 4 agents listed, and correctly identified security-auditor and auth-debugger as having security/authentication mentions. Now I need to create the summary.txt file.",
  "plan": "Create summary.txt with a human-readable summary of the audit results.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' 'Agent Audit Summary' '==================' '' 'Total agents discovered: 4' '' 'Agent List:' '  - security-auditor [SECURITY/AUTH]' '  - code-reviewer' '  - docs-helper' '  - auth-debugger [SECURITY/AUTH]' '' 'Agents with security/authentication mentions: 2' '  - security-auditor' '  - auth-debugger' > summary.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat summary.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la agent_audit.json summary.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Both required files have been successfully created:\n\n1. agent_audit.json - Contains the complete audit with 4 agents discovered, including their names, descriptions, paths, and security_auth flags. Correctly identified security-auditor and auth-debugger as having security/authentication mentions.\n\n2. summary.txt - Human-readable summary showing total agents, the agent list with security flags, and the list of flagged agents.\n\nThe task used the registry.json file as the registry data source (rather than scanning agent folders directly) as instructed.",
  "plan": "Task is complete. Both agent_audit.json and summary.txt have been created with the correct content.",
  "commands": [],
  "task_complete": true
}
